Draws on
--------
Recomputing every claim from the raw facts, instead of trusting a stored headline, draws on the Guided
Entropy Principle (GEP) result that a stable system can stabilize a wrong reference. The typed verdict with
a fingerprint over the canonical result follows the shape of that paper's proposed audit receipt (a verdict
plus a hash of its derivation):

  Gary W. Floyd, Lumiea Systems Research Division — ThunderStruck Service LLC — "From GEP Stabilization
  to Dual-Map Ethical Reasoning: A derivation of positive ethical evidence, negative ethical evidence, and
  non-legal moral reasoning," Derivation v0.2. Open Defensive Prior Art (Creative Commons).

